A||||20||Fat||88 upper ball joints||||1||
Z||000000||Fat||02-12-2001||09:01 PM||||Hey dare, I'm looking for a set of upper balljoints for my 88 GT.  I found, by using the search function, only the Fiero Store has them, and their $58 a side!  Seems a little crazy to me because I just bought the lowers at Advanced today for $38 a side, and the Fiero Store wants even more for those than the uppers.  They've got 160k miles on them, so their probably pretty worn.  I replaced the lowers about 35k ago, but as these parts are getting more and more rare, I see the $80 I spent today as an investment.  From now on I'm not going to throw away a single suspension part.  We're probably going to have to fabricate these in the near future.  <P>Also, does anyone have any input on what to replace on a major suspension overhaul?  And what are the best (cheapest) sources for each part?<P>Thanks, from the new fat guy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||02-12-2001||09:39 PM||||I bought most of all the ball joints and tie rod ends at Carport. It took a few days, but everything was there. Not a "name" brand, but it was the best they could get. Oh, the inner rods, rack bellows and rack bushing came from Rodney. I would check with him and see what all he has. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||02-12-2001||10:06 PM||||If the Fiero Store didn't sell upper ball joints, many of us would be SOL!<P>BTW, who is "dare"?<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||Fat||02-12-2001||10:54 PM||||Hey dare Cooter, I looked up rodneydickman.com and found the parts you listed.<P>inner tie rods: $27 ea<BR>bellows: $15 ea<BR>rack bushing: $19<P>He says the rack bushing was originally plastic, so was yours worn out when you replaced it?  Did this steering rack rebuild significantly improve the feel of your car?  My GT feels like it has a bumpsteer problem, almost like the balljoints are gone.  The front tires are cupped bad, but the alignment checked out okay.  I'm going to replace the bushing with poly and put new kyb shocks on all corners.  Is there anything else you did that I may overlook?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fat||02-13-2001||04:31 PM||||Hey dare, back again.  I ordered some brake parts today.  Loaded calipers are $35 at Advanced, so I bought two.  The core is $55 each though.  It came out to $200 with tax, so I need to get this project done ASAP to get some of my money back.  I'm going to try to rebuild the back one's first.  Hopefully they're not too worn.  <P>Who supplies poly bushings at the best price.  I'm gonna need the whole shootin' match, back and front including endlinks and swaybar brackets.  This thing is gonna be stiff, the car that is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||02-13-2001||05:34 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A>  <P>Best source for poly<P>I am still wondering who dare is...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||Quadfiero||02-13-2001||08:14 PM||||I found the upper ball joints at Partamerica.com. You can get most of the parts at Advanced Autoparts. They didn't have the part number for that particular manufacturer but an alert manager recognized a number on the print out as a TRW part number. That is what I bought. The price was about $25.<BR>Hope that helps. I'll see if I can't find the part number.<BR>Bob <BR>'88 Fiero GT Quad 4 HO<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Quadfiero||02-13-2001||08:16 PM||||I misspelled Partsamerica.com<BR>Sorry||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||02-13-2001||08:54 PM||||You will get '84-'87 upper balljoints from Partsamerica/Advance Auto, etc.  I already tried buying the uppers from them a few months ago.  I had to special order them......when they arrived they were for the earlier Fieros.  I had the guy call the warehouse to figure things out and he even went so far as to call McQuay-Norris (which makes them) and they don't show them as available.<P>Call the Fiero Store or get them through GM (last I heard they were still available).<P><BR>Black88GT.......when he says "dare" he means "there" (think Cajun accent), so Hey dare would be Hey there.   You got dat??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    <P>I guess those two years in Louisiana paid off.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
