Z||000011||Quadfiero||02-14-2001||03:32 PM||||Thanks for the heads up Mrfiero,<BR>     I found the part TRW part number and checked the application. The number, TRW 10326 is for the earlier Fieros. I found a Rare parts part number 10772 but I don't know who carries that brand. Anyone have any ideas? <BR>     Bummer, I was going to install them this weekend. What a surprise that would have been. <BR>Thanks,<BR>Bob<BR>I'll let you know if I find them. I'll make sure they give me the correct ones first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Quadfiero||02-14-2001||03:51 PM||||Well, I talked to Rare parts rep. Good news, they have them. The bad news, $73.04. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||GT GT 87||02-14-2001||06:35 PM||||Listen,,,Don't be so foolish on parts that , if you buy quality- it will last longer that oem...  Buy Moog  Buy Moog  You will have to look for a dealer but that is what NASCAR uses. I bought up and low B-joints for my last GT (86) at pep boys because they were the cheapest , but I saw they were not grooved to let the grease into the rubber boot.These things squeaked forever ,when I turned ,or when I even leaned on a fender.    My dream is to get to an '88 with the beter suspension ,keep it mint!!!!!       Steve||||reg||1
